('area:paradiski','pass','line',15,'{{diff:F000065,F000264}}',array['F000065','F000264']::text[],'review','loader','pass.table.rows.3.3'),
('area:paradiski','pass','note',0,'Sources: <a href="https://guide-ski.fr/?p=1230">Guide Ski</a> for La Plagne, <a href="https://www.lesarcs-peiseyvallandry.com/en/forfaits_offre">Les Arcs and Peisey-Vallandry</a>, and <a href="https://www.alti-mag.com/tarifs-forfaits-de-ski/tarifs-forfaits-ski-alpes/tarifs-forfaits-ski-alpes-du-nord">Alti-Mag</a> for the Paradiski pass, at the same prices the two resorts publish.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.table.note'),
('area:paradiski','pass','heading',1,'What the pass covers','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.coverageTitle'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',16,'Linked both ways by lift and piste','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.coverage.0.label'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',17,'La Plagne, with Montalbert, Champagny-en-Vanoise and Montchavin-Les Coches','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.coverage.0.items.0'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',18,'Les Arcs, with Arc 1600, Arc 1800, Arc 1950, Arc 2000 and Villaroger','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.coverage.0.items.1'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',19,'Peisey-Vallandry','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.coverage.0.items.2'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',20,'Reached from the valley by funicular','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.coverage.1.label'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',21,'Bourg-Saint-Maurice, by the Arc en Ciel funicular to Arc 1600','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.coverage.1.items.0'),
('area:paradiski','pass','heading',2,'Which pass for which trip','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenariosTitle'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',22,'A week in La Plagne','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.0.who'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',23,'The Paradiski pass costs {{diff:F000066,F000258}} more, and from Plagne Bellecôte, Arc 1800 is {{m:all.bellecote.arc-1800|w}} lift rides away.',array['F000066','F000258']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.0.what'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',24,'A week in Les Arcs','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.1.who'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',25,'The Paradiski pass costs {{diff:F000066,F000265}} more; from Arc 1800, Plagne Centre takes {{m:all.arc-1800.plagne-centre|w}} lift rides, so La Plagne is a full day out.',array['F000066','F000265']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.1.what'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',26,'Families','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.2.who'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',27,'A child''s six day Paradiski pass costs {{f:F000267}}. The Pack Famille takes {{f:F000270}} off each pass when two adults and at least two children buy four Paradiski passes of six to eight days together.',array['F000267','F000270']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.2.what'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',28,'Early season','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.3.who'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',29,'From {{f:F000262|dm}} to {{f:F000263|dm}} the six day La Plagne pass falls to {{f:F000261}}.',array['F000261','F000262','F000263']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.3.what'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',30,'Late season','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.4.who'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',31,'After {{f:F000224|dm}} the Vanoise Express has stopped, and a local pass covers all the skiing that can be reached on skis.',array['F000224']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.4.what'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',32,'Extras','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.5.who'),
('area:paradiski','pass','line',33,'The Premium pass from Les Arcs costs {{diff:F000269,F000066}} more than the standard Paradiski week and includes unlimited sledging on the Luge 1800 and the Luge 2000.',array['F000066','F000269']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.5.what'),
('area:paradiski','pass','note',1,'On the La Plagne prices, children are 5 to 12 and seniors 65 to 74, and both pay the child rate. The season opens on {{f:F000225}}.',array['F000225']::text[],'review','loader','pass.after'),
('area:paradiski','access','heading',0,'Getting there and choosing a base','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.h2'),
('area:paradiski','access','para',0,'By the fastest road, Geneva airport is {{f:F000367}} from Champagny-en-Vanoise and {{f:F000368}} from Arc 2000, the nearest and farthest of the villages; Lyon airport is {{f:F000369|n}} to {{f:F000370}} away and Chambéry {{f:F000371|n}} to {{f:F000372}}. Every route ends on the RN90 up the Tarentaise valley, and the resorts'' own roads climb from Moûtiers, Aime and Bourg-Saint-Maurice.',array['F000367','F000368','F000369','F000370','F000371','F000372']::text[],'review','loader','access.paras.0'),
('area:paradiski','access','para',1,'The railway follows the same valley. This winter the Eurostar ski service from London runs as two trains with a change at Lille, and outbound on Saturdays it calls at Aime-la-Plagne, Moûtiers and Bourg-Saint-Maurice. At Bourg the Arc en Ciel funicular climbs to Arc 1600 in {{f:F000252|w}} minutes, and passengers arriving by train ride it both ways free on the day they arrive.',array['F000252']::text[],'review','loader','access.paras.1'),
('area:paradiski','access','note',0,'Road distances are the fastest route by the OSRM router on OpenStreetMap data, without traffic or snow. The ski train as reported by <a href="https://www.seat61.com/trains-and-routes/eurostar-ski-train.htm">Seat 61</a>; the funicular by <a href="https://guide-ski.fr/?p=4292">Guide Ski</a>. 2026/27 bus timetables have not yet been checked.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.accessNote'),
('area:paradiski','access','heading',1,'How far each base reaches','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.basesH3'),
('area:paradiski','access','para',2,'Which side of the Vanoise Express a skier sleeps on shapes the week more than the pass does. Plagne Bellecôte is the best placed for both halves, {{f:F000296|w}} lift rides from Plagne Centre and {{f:F000297|w}} from Arc 1800. Peisey-Vallandry and Montchavin-Les Coches sit at the two ends of the cable car, yet from Peisey, Plagne Centre is still {{f:F000320|w}} lift rides away.',array['F000296','F000297','F000320']::text[],'review','loader','access.basesParas.0'),
('area:paradiski','access','para',3,'The corners pay for their quiet in lifts. From Montalbert, Arc 2000 takes {{f:F000282|w}} lift rides, and from Villaroger, Plagne Centre takes {{f:F000352|w}}. Arc 2000 is the base for the highest skiing, with a lift top above 3,000 m {{f:F000347|w}} rides from the village.',array['F000282','F000347','F000352']::text[],'review','loader','access.basesParas.1'),
('area:paradiski','access','caption',0,'Lift rides from each base','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.basesCaption'),
('area:paradiski','access','line',0,'To Plagne Centre','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.baseCols.0'),
