('area:paradiski','access','line',10,'Arc 1600','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.bases.6.base'),
('area:paradiski','access','line',11,'Montalbert','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.bases.7.base'),
('area:paradiski','access','line',12,'Champagny-en-Vanoise','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.bases.8.base'),
('area:paradiski','access','line',13,'Villaroger','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.bases.9.base'),
('area:paradiski','access','note',1,'Fewest lift rides from the village lifts before reaching the first lift of each area, on the OpenStreetMap model. Times are not included.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.basesNote'),
('area:paradiski','snowboard','kicker',0,'Snowboarders','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.kicker'),
('area:paradiski','snowboard','heading',0,'Riding Paradiski on a board','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.h2'),
('area:paradiski','snowboard','para',0,'Each resort keeps its own parks. Les Arcs has the SPARK Snowpark at Arc 1600 and a boardercross at the Col de la Chal on the Arc 2000 side. La Plagne has the Riders Nation park, the Funslope in Plagne Bellecôte, which Guide Ski calls the longest of its kind in Europe, the Buffalo Park and a lit tunnel called the Equalizer, with boardercross courses at Champagny-en-Vanoise and Montchavin-Les Coches.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.paras.0'),
('area:paradiski','snowboard','para',1,'Drag lifts are where the two resorts differ. In the map data {{f:F000273}} of the {{f:F000272}} main lifts are drags. They make up {{f:F000279}} of the main lifts in Montalbert and {{f:F000287}} in Plagne Centre, against {{f:F000335}} in Arc 1800 and {{f:F000295}} in Plagne Bellecôte, which makes Les Arcs and the Bellecôte bowl the easier bases on a board.',array['F000272','F000273','F000279','F000287','F000295','F000335']::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.paras.1'),
('area:paradiski','snowboard','para',2,'Away from the parks, the run from the Aiguille Rouge down to Villaroger is the long ride of the area, {{f:F000254}} with more than {{f:F000255}} of descent. Terrain beyond the markers is not controlled, so the avalanche bulletin and a local guide come first.',array['F000254','F000255']::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.paras.2'),
('area:paradiski','snowboard','heading',1,'Parks and places to ride','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.listTitle'),
('area:paradiski','snowboard','note',0,'Parks: <a href="https://guide-ski.fr/?p=4292">Guide Ski for Les Arcs</a> and <a href="https://guide-ski.fr/?p=1230">for La Plagne</a>; the Champagny boardercross route: <a href="https://www.igluski.com/blog/post/best-mountain-restaurants-la-plagne">Iglu Ski</a>; the Aiguille Rouge run: <a href="https://www.lesarcs.com/en/node/2770/aiguille-rouge">Les Arcs</a>. Drag lift shares from OpenStreetMap. Park layouts change every season.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.note'),
('area:paradiski','families','kicker',0,'Families','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.kicker'),
('area:paradiski','families','heading',0,'Holidays with children','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.h2'),
('area:paradiski','families','para',0,'France.fr lists Montalbert and Montchavin under Famille Plus, the national label for family resorts, and both are among the lower villages of La Plagne. The Pack Famille on the Paradiski pass and the child rate for seniors help on the price.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.paras.0'),
('area:paradiski','families','para',1,'La Plagne does most for beginners. The CoolSki areas have free lifts and marked circuits, Buffalo Kids is a play area on the snow for children, and Belle Plagne has a Family Spa with an outdoor pool at 35°C. The bobsleigh track built for the {{f:F000240}} Olympics, the only one in France, takes passengers in winter.',array['F000240']::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.paras.1'),
('area:paradiski','families','para',2,'Les Arcs has learner areas in Arc 1800, Arc 2000 and Vallandry, with the Piste des Minis in Arc 1800 and the Forêt des Pitchouns in Vallandry for the smallest skiers. The Luge 1800 and the Luge 2000 sledging runs are included without limit on the Premium pass, and Arc 1800 has the swimming pool, La Piscine.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.paras.2'),
('area:paradiski','families','para',3,'For a base, Plagne Bellecôte has the highest share of green and blue in the map data, {{f:F000294}}, and sits within easy reach of both resorts; Guide Ski finds the most services and activities of the Arc villages in Arc 1800.',array['F000294']::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.paras.3'),
('area:paradiski','families','heading',1,'For children','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.listTitle'),
('area:paradiski','families','note',0,'Sources: <a href="https://www.france.fr/fr/article/label-ski-famille-plus/">France.fr on Famille Plus</a> (updated October 2023), <a href="https://guide-ski.fr/?p=1230">Guide Ski for La Plagne</a> and <a href="https://guide-ski.fr/?p=4292">for Les Arcs</a>, <a href="https://www.inthesnow.com/la-plagne/for-families/">InTheSnow</a> (2022) and <a href="https://www.lesarcs-peiseyvallandry.com/en/forfaits_offre">Les Arcs lift passes</a>. Ages and opening times are best checked when booking.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.note'),
('area:paradiski','food','kicker',0,'Food','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.kicker'),
('area:paradiski','food','heading',0,'Eating on the mountain','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.h2'),
('area:paradiski','food','para',0,'Paradiski has no Michelin star in the 2026 guide, and its pleasures are terraces and the farm cooking of Savoie rather than tasting menus. Between Belle Plagne and Champagny, the Roc des Blanchets has a south facing terrace reached on gentle blues. On the Bellecôte side the Chalet des Colosses, with a red British phone box outside, is known for its vegetarian dishes as well as its fondue, and Les Inversens near the top of the Roche de Mio has a terrace big enough for large groups.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.paras.0'),
('area:paradiski','food','para',1,'Lower down, the Chalet de la Roche in Plagne 1500, at the foot of the bobsleigh track, is the stop for pizza, and the Chalet du Friolin at the bottom of the Bauches lift in Montchavin sets out deckchairs on its terrace.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.paras.1'),
('area:paradiski','food','para',2,'Les Arcs has the more storied tables. Belliou La Fumée occupies a hunting lodge built for Victor Emmanuel of Italy and cooks over a fire, and Les Chalets de l''Arc in Arc 2000 bakes its own bread. L''Ancolie, in the hamlet of Nancroix, is reached with a guide on the off piste Rosset route and left by shuttle bus. Down in Le Pré, La Ferme serves fondue at the end of the run from the Aiguille Rouge.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.paras.2'),
('area:paradiski','food','heading',1,'Tables worth the detour','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.listTitle'),
('area:paradiski','food','note',0,'Michelin 2026: <a href="https://presse.explore-savoie.com/les-tables-distinguees-2026/">Savoie tourism</a>. Restaurants: <a href="https://www.igluski.com/blog/post/best-mountain-restaurants-la-plagne">Iglu Ski</a> for La Plagne and <a href="https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/les-arcs/les-arcs-eat-drink-party">Snowcarbon</a> for Les Arcs. Restaurants change hands and menus each season.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.note'),
('area:paradiski','apres','kicker',0,'Après','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.kicker'),
('area:paradiski','apres','heading',0,'Après and evenings','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.h2'),
('area:paradiski','apres','para',0,'The loudest afternoon is at La Folie Douce, at the top of the Villards gondola above Arc 1800 since {{f:F000256}}, with an open air show from two in the afternoon and DJs from three until five.',array['F000256']::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.paras.0'),
('area:paradiski','apres','para',1,'In Arc 2000, El Latino Loco is the liveliest bar, with live music and fajitas, and Red Rock serves burgers. Arc 1950 has The Wool Sock''s Pub on the snow, and Le Carré is the club for dancing until morning.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.paras.1'),
('area:paradiski','apres','para',2,'La Plagne''s evenings are spread across its villages. In Plagne Soleil, Monica''s Pub sits beside the Bergerie lift with a big sunny terrace, live music and DJs. In Plagne Centre, Igloo Igloo has live music and DJ sets and Bar Fort Colorado stands by the Colorado chair, while La Mine Bar in Plagne 1800 is an English style pub with live sport.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.paras.2'),
('area:paradiski','apres','heading',1,'Where the evenings start','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.listTitle'),
('area:paradiski','apres','note',0,'Sources: <a href="https://www.seelaplagne.com/news/la-folie-douce-lands-in-la-plagne-winter-201920-la-plagne-region-729376">See La Plagne on La Folie Douce</a> (October 2019), <a href="https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/les-arcs/les-arcs-eat-drink-party">Snowcarbon</a> for Les Arcs and <a href="https://www.seelaplagne.com/nightlife/apres/apres-ski-in-la-plagne">See La Plagne</a> for La Plagne (October 2026). Bars open and close from season to season.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.note'),
('area:paradiski','fit','heading',0,'Who it suits','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.h2'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',0,'How the area suits different kinds of trip, on the evidence gathered so far.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.intro'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',1,'Exploring a large network','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.0.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',2,'Good fit','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.0.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',3,'Ten sectors share one pass, all linked by lift and piste, with the Vanoise Express between the two resorts.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.0.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',4,'Everything between the two halves depends on one cable car, and Montalbert to Villaroger takes {{m:all.montalbert.villaroger|w}} lift rides.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.0.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',5,'Intermediates who want variety','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.1.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',6,'Good fit','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.1.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',7,'Green and blue reach every sector in the map data, and reds never shorten a journey.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.1.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',8,'From the corners, crossing to the other resort takes most of a day.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.1.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',9,'Groups of mixed ability','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.2.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',10,'Good fit','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.2.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',11,'From Plagne Bellecôte both resorts are close, so a group can split and meet again for lunch.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.2.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',12,'A meeting point on the wrong side of the cable car can mean a long way home.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.2.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',13,'First timers','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.3.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',14,'Good fit','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.3.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',15,'CoolSki areas with free lifts in La Plagne, and learner areas in Arc 1800, Arc 2000 and Vallandry.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.3.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',16,'The Paradiski pass is wasted on a first week; the local passes cost {{diff:F000066,F000258}} to {{diff:F000066,F000265}} less.',array['F000066','F000258','F000265']::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.3.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',17,'Families','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.4.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',18,'Good fit','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.4.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',19,'Famille Plus in Montalbert and Montchavin, the Pack Famille discount, and play areas and pools in both resorts.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.4.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',20,'Prices for lessons and childcare vary by village and are best checked when booking.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.4.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',21,'Snowboarders','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.5.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',22,'Mixed','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.5.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',23,'Parks and boardercross in both resorts, and few drags in Arc 1800 and Plagne Bellecôte.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.5.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',24,'Drags make up {{f:F000279}} of the main lifts in Montalbert and {{f:F000287}} in Plagne Centre.',array['F000279','F000287']::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.5.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',25,'Experts','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.6.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',26,'Mixed','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.6.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',27,'{{f:F000238}} black runs in Les Arcs and Peisey-Vallandry and the long descent from the Aiguille Rouge to Villaroger.',array['F000238']::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.6.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',28,'skiresort.com rates only {{f:F000077}} of the piste as difficult.',array['F000077']::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.6.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',29,'Putting snow first','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.7.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',30,'Mixed','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.7.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',31,'Arc 2000 and Plagne Bellecôte ski high, and the Aiguille Rouge and Glaciers lifts reach above 3,000 m.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.7.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',32,'At 1,600 m all of the last five modelled seasons were poor, and the low sectors of La Plagne close a week early.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.7.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',33,'Travelling without a car','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.8.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',34,'Good fit','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.8.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',35,'The ski train calls at Aime-la-Plagne and Bourg-Saint-Maurice, and the funicular from Bourg to Arc 1600 is free on the day of arrival.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.8.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',36,'2026/27 timetables have not yet been checked.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.8.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',37,'Preferring a smaller area','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.9.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',38,'Mixed','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.9.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',39,'Local passes cover La Plagne, or Les Arcs and Peisey-Vallandry, on their own.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.9.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',40,'Each half is a large area in itself.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.9.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',41,'Food lovers','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.10.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',42,'Mixed','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.10.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',43,'Farm cooking, sunny terraces and a lunch reached off piste at L''Ancolie.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.10.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',44,'There is no Michelin star in the area in the 2026 guide.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.10.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',45,'Looking for après','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.11.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',46,'Good fit','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.11.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',47,'La Folie Douce above Arc 1800 and busy bars in Arc 2000, Arc 1950 and Plagne Soleil.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.11.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',48,'The evenings are spread thinly across many villages.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.11.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',49,'Non skiers','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.12.who'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',50,'Mixed','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.12.fit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',51,'The Olympic bobsleigh track, sledging runs, pools in Arc 1800 and Belle Plagne, and the Vanoise Express itself.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.12.why'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',52,'Each activity is paid for separately unless it comes with the Premium pass.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.rows.12.limit'),
('area:paradiski','fit','heading',1,'The catches','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.catchesH3'),
('area:paradiski','fit','line',53,'The catches come from the shape of the area. Everything between the two resorts hangs on the Vanoise Express, which stops a week before the season ends, and from the corners the far side is a long day away: Montalbert to Villaroger takes {{m:all.montalbert.villaroger|w}} lift rides. The older sectors of La Plagne lean on drag lifts, and the lower villages have lost the most snow, with all of the last five modelled seasons at 1,600 m in the lowest third.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','fit.catches'),
('area:paradiski','compare','heading',0,'The other large areas of Savoie','{}'::text[],'review','loader','compare.h2'),
('area:paradiski','compare','para',0,'Set against its neighbours, Paradiski is second in size only to Les 3 Vallées, with {{f:F000071}} of piste against {{f:F000002}} and about a fifth fewer lifts. Its day ticket costs the same as Tignes Val d''Isère''s, {{f:F000065}}, and its six day pass less than either Les 3 Vallées or Tignes Val d''Isère.',array['F000002','F000065','F000071']::text[],'review','loader','compare.paras.0'),
('area:paradiski','compare','para',1,'Paradiski starts lower than Tignes Val d''Isère, at {{f:F000073}} against {{f:F000082}}, and tops out lower, at {{f:F000074}} against {{f:F000083}}. Its grade split is close to that of Les 3 Vallées, and in the weather model it has a little more snow at 1,600 m than either Les 3 Vallées or Tignes Val d''Isère. Les Sybelles is cheaper and snowier at that height but tops out at {{f:F000092}}.',array['F000073','F000074','F000082','F000083','F000092']::text[],'review','loader','compare.paras.1'),
('area:paradiski','compare','caption',0,'Four linked areas of Savoie','{}'::text[],'review','loader','compare.caption'),
