('area:paradiski','method','line',0,'Which resorts count','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.0.dt'),
('area:paradiski','method','line',1,'The three resorts the operator names, La Plagne, Les Arcs and Peisey-Vallandry, split into the ten sectors that a skier meets on the ground. Sharing the pass is recorded separately from being linked by lift and piste.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.0.dd'),
('area:paradiski','method','line',2,'How links were checked','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.1.dt'),
('area:paradiski','method','line',3,'A sector counts as linked only when a route of lifts and pistes reaches it in the OpenStreetMap data. Drag lifts run one way and gondolas may be ridden down. The Vanoise Express runs two cabins on parallel tracks and is counted as one lift. A link is critical when closing one lift on it cuts routes that no other lift replaces. Tignes, La Rosière and Sainte-Foy-Tarentaise are left out of the model. The model has not yet been checked against the official 2026/27 piste map.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.1.dd'),
('area:paradiski','method','line',4,'Piste totals','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.2.dt'),
('area:paradiski','method','line',5,'Operator and measured figures are both shown and never averaged. Mapped piste from OpenStreetMap is used only to compare sectors and grades.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.2.dd'),
('area:paradiski','method','line',6,'Comparisons','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.3.dt'),
('area:paradiski','method','line',7,'The four areas compared use the same source for each row, so a figure can be set against its neighbour.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.3.dd'),
