('area:paradiski','method','heading',0,'Figures that do not agree','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.conflictsH3'),
('area:paradiski','method','line',52,'skiresort.com counts {{f:F000072}} lifts across Paradiski, while Guide Ski gives {{f:F000231}} for La Plagne and {{f:F000234}} for Les Arcs and Peisey-Vallandry. The elevation model puts the Aiguille Rouge cable car at {{f:F000341}} against the operator''s {{f:F000221}}, and the Glaciers gondola at {{f:F000293}} against {{f:F000232}}. The mapped piste comes to {{f:F000275}}, against {{f:F000071}} on the listings. The modelled snowfall at 1,600 m is {{f:F000361}} on this page, while an earlier run for the same grid cell gave a slightly higher figure, and the difference is being checked. This page names each source alongside its figure.',array['F000071','F000072','F000221','F000231','F000232','F000234','F000275','F000293','F000341','F000361']::text[],'review','loader','method.conflicts'),
('area:paradiski','method','line',53,'Research of 24 October 2026. Size, runs and resorts: <a href="https://www.paradiski.com/en">Paradiski</a>. Lifts, runs, season dates, parks and passes: <a href="https://guide-ski.fr/?p=1230">Guide Ski for La Plagne</a>, <a href="https://guide-ski.fr/?p=4292">Guide Ski for Les Arcs</a>, <a href="https://www.skipass-laplagne.com/en/tarifs-publics">La Plagne lift passes</a> and <a href="https://www.lesarcs-peiseyvallandry.com/en/forfaits_offre">Les Arcs lift passes</a>. Measured size and grades: skiresort.com for <a href="https://www.skiresort.com/en/ski-resort/la-plagne-paradiski/">La Plagne</a> and <a href="https://www.skiresort.com/en/ski-resort/les-arcs-peisey-vallandry-paradiski/">Les Arcs</a>. History and the Vanoise Express: Wikipedia on <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Plagne">La Plagne</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Arcs">Les Arcs</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanoise_Express">the Vanoise Express</a>. Network, bases, routes and lift heights: a graph of {{f:F000271}} lifts and {{f:F000274}} piste sections from <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a> (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL), with heights from the Copernicus 90 m elevation model via <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/elevation-api">Open-Meteo</a>. Snowfall: ERA5 reanalysis via the <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/historical-weather-api">Open-Meteo historical weather API</a> (CC BY 4.0). Road distances: <a href="https://project-osrm.org/">OSRM</a>. Facts from operators, measurements, model results and estimates are kept apart in the research files, and conflicting figures are listed above rather than averaged.',array['F000271','F000274']::text[],'review','loader','method.sources');
